WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.552
Before pivoting admissions, inspect the long source.

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:05.527
Each admission is a row.

00:00:05.527 --> 00:00:09.602
Diagnosis is stored as a value, not as a column.

00:00:09.602 --> 00:00:13.957
The pivot will create separate diagnosis count columns by month.

00:00:13.957 --> 00:00:19.072
Understanding the source grain makes the later GROUP BY easier to interpret.

00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:25.552
Long and wide are not labels for good and bad design; they are shapes suited to different tasks.

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:31.112
Long data is often easier for grouping, plotting, and scalable storage.

00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:37.622
Wide data is often convenient for human-readable reports or some modeling interfaces.

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:40.411
Choose the shape required by the next step.
